From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rothko Port Maintainers <rothko-port@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] java: optionally share highmem pool across local JVM actions

Memory-constrained local builds can enter sustained reclaim while many
4/8 GiB JVM compilers run at once. NINJA_HIGHMEM_NUM_JOBS alone does not
cover ordinary javac, Kotlin, turbine and dex rules.

Opt in with SOONG_JAVA_HIGHMEM_POOL=true and set the existing highmem pool
depth through NINJA_HIGHMEM_NUM_JOBS. Keep native concurrency unchanged.
Include signing, jar transforms, lint, Javadoc and Metalava JVM actions.
Preserve default and remote-build scheduling. Test actual generated Ninja
rules with the switch on/off and remote configuration on/off.

---
